msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/logging.rst:122
msgid "Using Third-Party Loggers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/logging.rst:124
msgid ""
"You can use any other logger that you might like as long as it extends "
"from either ``Psr\\Log\\LoggerInterface`` and is `PSR-3 <https://www.php-"
"fig.org/psr/psr-3/>`_ compatible. This means that you can easily drop in "
"use for any PSR-3 compatible logger, or create your own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/logging.rst:128
msgid ""
"You must ensure that the third-party logger can be found by the system, "
"by adding it to either the **app/Config/Autoload.php** configuration "
"file, or through another autoloader, like Composer. Next, you should "
"modify **app/Config/Services.php** to point the ``logger`` alias to your "
"new class name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/logging.rst:133
msgid ""
"Now, any call that is done through the :php:func:`log_message()` function"
" will use your library instead."
msgstr ""

